{"slug":"cpi-2024-food-classes-groups","path":"official","kind":"timeseries","page_url":"https://esankhyiki.mospi.gov.in/macroindicators?product=cpi","frequency":"M","graph":"line","title":"CPI (Base 2024=100): Food Classes, Cereals, Pulses, Vegetables and Selected Groups","description":"Detailed price indices from MoSPI's new CPI (2024=100), monthly, all-India, rural/urban/combined: the nine food classes (cereals, meat, fish, milk & eggs, oils & fats, fruit, vegetables-and-pulses, sugar, ready-made food), the sub-classes 'Cereals', 'Pulses' and five vegetable sub-classes, and selected groups (food, beverages, clothing, footwear, actual rent, electricity/gas/other fuels, personal transport, passenger transport, information & communication services, medicines, outpatient care). Food-price detail matters for nowcasting because food swings drive headline CPI. The new classification has no single 'vegetables' index: vegetables are split into five sub-classes and combined with pulses in one class. Fuel and light is not a group any more (electricity, gas and fuels are one group inside housing). The new CPI (base 2024=100, MoSPI, first released 12 Feb 2026 for January 2026) replaced the 2012-base series. It uses the COICOP-2018 classification (12 divisions) and a 358-item basket weighted from the 2023-24 Household Consumption Expenditure Survey, so its groups are NOT comparable with the old Food/Fuel/Clothing/Housing/Miscellaneous groups and it has no 'core' aggregate. Index values start in January 2025 (the base year). Do not chain this series to the 2012-base series.","headline":{},"source":"MoSPI (eSankhyiki CPI, base 2024=100)","source_url":"https://esankhyiki.mospi.gov.in/macroindicators?product=cpi","date_modified":null,"views":[{"id":"class_combined","label":"Food classes - Combined","series":[{"id":"class_combined_0","name":"Cereals and cereal products","units":"Index (2024=100)","pts":[[1735689600,103.89],[1738368000,104.37],[1740787200,104.53],[1743465600,104.13]